<!--
  sce:std/shared/record_compact.scxml — the host's word that the changes of a copy of a
  shared record list (record_list) up to an instant are settled, so that it can forget
  them: `before`, a wall time in milliseconds. Every tombstone (a write someone wrote
  over) stamped at or before it is dropped, with the add it names, and leaves the digest.
  What the copy shows is unchanged: a register holds the values nobody has written over,
  and a value that was written over is not one of them.

  The host says it only when every copy has taken in every change stamped at or before
  `before` and none is still on its way: a copy that had not taken in a tombstone, or a
  write that arrives again after it, would hold an add nothing any longer says was written
  over, and the value would come back (orset_live). A server that keeps each device's read
  cursor knows it (stable_point); the host tells every copy the same instant. A host that
  does not know it asks the hub to settle instead (record_settle).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="record_compact"
       sce:event-name="record_list.compact">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="before" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
